shortname: "Ai Electronics ABC 24"
comment: 'CP/M; 158kB 35-track DSDD'
read_support_status: UNICORN

documentation:
<<<
Ai Electronics was a Japanese computer company that produced minicomputers during the 1960s and 1970s. In 1979 they
started production of the ABC, the Ai Business Computer, a decently specced CP/M machine with 64kB RAM, a Z80, twin
floppy drives, GBIP ports, and a maths coprocessor.

The floppy disks it uses are relatively normal 35-track IBM scheme disks, with cylinder 0 reserved as the boot track.
>>>

documentation:
<<<
## References

  - [DoPECC's page on the ABC 24](https://dopecc.net/computers/ai/)
>>>

image_reader {
  filename: "abc.img"
  type: IMAGETYPE_IMG
}

image_writer {
  filename: "abc.img"
  type: IMAGETYPE_IMG
}

flux_source {
  type: FLUXTYPE_DRIVE
}

encoder {
  ibm {
    trackdata {
      target_rotational_period_ms: 167
      target_clock_period_us: 3.333
    }
  }
}

decoder {
  ibm {
  }
}

layout {
  layoutdata {
    sector_size: 512
    physical {
      start_sector: 1
      count: 9
    }
  }
  tracks: 35
  sides: 2
  format_type: FORMATTYPE_40TRACK
}

filesystem {
	type: CPMFS
	cpmfs {
		filesystem_start {
			track: 1
			side: 0
			sector: 1
		}
		block_size: 2048
		dir_entries: 64
	}
}


